  rung 0  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma diag)   logL = -38.9375897585

=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -24.1491940078
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=0)   logL =     -14.7883957507
                                 sum  =     -38.9375897585
                                 joint=     -38.9375897585
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -38.9375897585)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -1.123e-12   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = -32.1846810825
  rung 2  (F free, Theta free, Sigma free)   logL = -12.8900255172

